TenancyTransaction.commit() catches every error from db.transaction() and rethrows it as HostError CONFLICT with the message 'nothing was written'. It does not look at the error. When FeltDB answers COMMIT_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN or DURABILITY_FAILURE, the transaction may already have been applied. ArtifactHost.tenancy() awaits tx.commit() (host.ts:463), so the caller is told the membership or tenant change did not happen and that retrying is safe. A retried provision mints a fresh crypto.token tenant id and creates a second organization or membership. The collections path maps the same FeltDB codes to OUTCOME_UNKNOWN (collections.ts commitError, lines 191-196); the tenancy path does not. The new test simulates an authority that applies the write and then loses the acknowledgement: the write lands, yet commit() rejects with code CONFLICT and 'nothing was written'.

**Severity:** medium

### Evidence

1. [`packages/appboundry-host/src/tenancy.ts` lines 76–80](https://github.com/rkendel1/appboundry/blob/cd32300380a6ac5735b02891218f56814dfa8ac5/packages/appboundry-host/src/tenancy.ts#L76-L80):

```
    try {
      await this.#db.transaction({ operations } as never);
    } catch (error) {
      throw new HostError("CONFLICT", `The membership change conflicted with a concurrent one; nothing was written. (${(error as Error).message})`);
    }
```

2. [`packages/appboundry-host/src/collections.ts` lines 191–192](https://github.com/rkendel1/appboundry/blob/cd32300380a6ac5735b02891218f56814dfa8ac5/packages/appboundry-host/src/collections.ts#L191-L192):

```
  if (error.code === FeltDBErrorCode.COMMIT_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN || error.code === FeltDBErrorCode.DURABILITY_FAILURE) {
    return new HostError("OUTCOME_UNKNOWN", `FeltDB could not confirm the commit (${error.code}); the mutation may or may not have been written.`, {
```

3. `test packages/appboundry-host/test/tenancy-commit-outcome.test.ts` fails on its assertions at cd32300380a6.

### Reproduction

<details><summary><code>packages/appboundry-host/test/tenancy-commit-outcome.test.ts</code> (fails today)</summary>

```ts
/**
 * A tenancy@1 commit whose outcome FeltDB could not confirm must not be reported as a conflict in which
 * nothing was written: the write may have landed, and a caller that retries a provision on that answer
 * creates a second organization (a fresh crypto.token id each time).
 */
import { describe, expect, it } from "vitest";
import { FeltDBErrorCode } from "@feltdb/core";
import { TenancyTransaction } from "../src/tenancy.js";

function fakeDb() {
  const written: unknown[] = [];
  const db = {
    collection: () => ({ get: async () => null }),
    query: async () => ({ records: [], exhausted: true }),
    // The authority applies the transaction, then the acknowledgement is lost.
    transaction: async (request: { operations: unknown[] }) => {
      written.push(...request.operations);
      throw Object.assign(new Error("commit outcome unknown"), { code: FeltDBErrorCode.COMMIT_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN });
    }
  };
  return { db, written };
}

describe("tenancy@1 commit outcome", () => {
  it("does not report an unconfirmed commit as a conflict that wrote nothing", async () => {
    const { db, written } = fakeDb();
    const tx = new TenancyTransaction(db as never);
    expect(await tx.get("_feltkit_tenants", "t1")).toBeNull();
    tx.create("_feltkit_tenants", "t1", { name: "Acme" });
    const error = (await tx.commit().then(() => null, e => e)) as { code?: string; message?: string } | null;
    expect(error).not.toBeNull();
    expect(written.length).toBe(1);
    // The record was written; the host must not tell the caller it was not.
    expect(error!.code).not.toBe("CONFLICT");
    expect(error!.message).not.toMatch(/nothing was written/);
  });
});

```
</details>

### Suggested fix

In TenancyTransaction.commit(), map FeltDB errors as commitError does. Only PRECONDITION_FAILED becomes CONFLICT ('nothing was written'). COMMIT_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN and DURABILITY_FAILURE become OUTCOME_UNKNOWN, with a hint to read before retrying. Contract violations and refusals keep their own codes, for example via feltdbRefusal/feltdbFailure. Also pass a stable transactionId so FeltDB can deduplicate a resend.

### How this was verified

- packages/appboundry-host/src/tenancy.ts:76-80 contains the quoted code
- packages/appboundry-host/src/collections.ts:191-192 contains the quoted code
- packages/appboundry-host/test/tenancy-commit-outcome.test.ts fails on its assertions at tree f89a99602225 (base cd32300380a6 plus tests)

Found and verified by Eve2 (task `mww5a689032ad2811ec6`, rkendel1/appboundry@cd32300380a6): the quoted lines were re-read and the reproduction re-run before filing.

